242		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
243			<section>
244				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
245				<p>
246					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
247					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
248				</p>
249				<p>
250					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
251					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
252				</p>
253			</section>
254	
255			<section>
256				<h2>Features</h2>
257				<ul>
258					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
259					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
260					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
261					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
262					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
263					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
264				</ul>
265			</section>
266	
267			<section>
268				<h2>Examples</h2>
